hich is the legal document explaining  the whole competition very detailedly  which we have published right now also  on our website  then as usual there's also a language  Criterium you need to speak to EU  languages one on Level C one at least  and one on level B2 at least  one of these two languages must be  English the other one can be any of the  23 remaining official EU languages  the selection procedure always looks  quite the same again if you would have  seen already tutorials of previous  competitions  the system looks quite alike so first  you have to apply of course and once you  have applied you will be invited to a  first stage of testing during which we  test the reading skills  the best performing will be invited to  the second stage which is an assessment  center during which we make you sit  three more tests  and then the successful candidates will  be listed on what we call the reserve  list and this is the basis for  recruitment by the different  institutions who will pick you and offer  you a job  so let's have a closer look to these  different steps as I said first of all  you need to apply how do you do that you  need an Excel account if you do not have  one yet you can create one on our  website very easily if you already have  one do use that account do not create a  second one because you're not allowed to  do so you can only have one account for  all your applications also for future  opportunities I always use that that  same account  you apply it on our website on the home  page you find the link to this  competition you can fill it out in any  other 24 official languages and you  should validate your application at the  latest on the 25th of October  uh prior to that time you can go in and  out your application as you wish as long  as you save your data nothing it gets  lost but at the end of course you need  to validate that application and by  sending it to us  um and that you can do only at or at the  latest on the 25th of October  everybody who applies will be invited to  this first step of reasoning skills now  since this competition has six different  fields  this stage is a bit different depending  on for which field you have applied so  as you can see this slide shows you the  reading skills procedure for Fields one  and two and then you'll see later on  there's a slight difference for the  fields three four five and six you see  there's a slight difference  what is the difference about for Fields  one and two so Finance or financial  management and accounting and Treasury  um there are as usual three tests to sit  numerical reasoning verbal reasoning and  abstract reasoning and for these two  Fields the numerical reasoning is  separate from the two others so you need  a separate pass score of 8 out of 15 in  this case for numerical reasoning  and then as you can see there is a  combined pass Mark for verbal and  abstract reasoning and there you need 12  out of 25 okay you set these reading  skills tests not in English so in your  other language all right  the difference for Fields three four  five and six is that here the verbal  reasoning is separate you need a  passcore of 10 out of 20 for your verbal  reasoning and then there is a combined  pass Mark for numerical and abstract  reasoning also the number of questions  and the duration and the scoring is a  bit different as you can see here but  all that is explained again in detail in  the notes of competition  I do advise you to train this well and  you can do so by having a look at our  sample test you see the link below on  this slide as well we offer sample tests  in all languages for you to train this  and if you train these kind of of  questions and and tests you will get  better at this so I really advise you to  go there and have a look if you think  about participating in this competition  I said the best performing will be  invited to a second stage  which is an assessment center and in the  assessment center we first test a set of  General competencies and then some also  field related competencies of course  so first a word about the general  competencies  um there are seven of them as you can  see on this slide here and we test these  competencies by or through two tests  there's a case study to be done which is  a written exercise  and this case study will test four  competencies as you can see here  and then you will set a situational  Competency Based interview which will  assess three more competencies this  interview is basically an interview  where we want to see how you react in a  given work related situation okay again  you will find sample tests on our sample  test page so again have a look there to  see what this looks like  the assessment center is always done in  English so all tests as from now will be  taken in English  for each competency you can get up to 10  points and you need a combined pass Mark  of 35 out of 70.  then of course we also test your field  related competency again in English and  that is based or done through an  interview you can get up to 100 points  here you need at least 50 and of course  the interview is related to one of these  six Fields the one that you have chosen  of course  the successful candidates are listed in  a big database and this is as I said in  the very beginning the the basis for  recruitment so once you are in this  database the different institutions will  consult this database and offer jobs to  different people on these lists and you  will be recruited in the months  following the publication of this list  the whole procedure can take up to 10  months so don't think that when you  apply now you will start working with us  in say January or so it's not the case  it takes quite long because as you may  know  we Select Staff from all over the EU so  we test these different candidates in  different languages  in different time slots most of the  tests actually actually all of the tests  can be taken remotely so you do not need  